---
.title = "Custom object handlers",
.date = .date("2026-09-16T00:00:00"),
.layout = "doc.shtml",
.translation_key = "advanced/handlers",
.custom = { "section": "Advanced topics" },
---

Ordinary PHP methods and properties cover most extensions. To change how Zend operates on an object, set `phpz.Class`'s `.handlers` to a set of `phpz.ObjectHandlers` overrides.

# [Choosing a handler entry point]($heading.id('choose-entry-point'))

| Operation | Preferred option |
| --- | --- |
| Initialize, destroy or clone Zig instance data | `.init`, `.deinit`, `.clone` |
| Report references to the garbage collector | `.gc` |
| Arithmetic and bitwise operations | `.operate` |
| Comparison | `.compare` |
| Other native object operations | Corresponding Zend callback in `.handlers` |

The instance-data options require a Zig struct with fields. Check callback signatures against your target PHP headers to avoid ABI mismatches.

# [Conflict rules]($heading.id('conflict-rules'))

Specifying both entries in any row produces a compile error.

| High-level option | Conflicting native handler |
| --- | --- |
| `.clone` | `.handlers.clone_obj` |
| `.gc` | `.handlers.get_gc` |
| `.operate` | `.handlers.do_operation` |
| `.compare` | `.handlers.compare` |

See [Object lifetime and garbage collection]($link.page('advanced/objects')) for cloning and GC, and [Operators and comparisons]($link.page('advanced/operators')) for operations and comparisons.

# [Property handler boundaries]($heading.id('property-handler-boundaries'))

`Object.property`, `setProperty` and `properties` can enter custom handlers or userland PHP. Keep scratch storage alive for temporary properties. Do not release a borrowed property table or edit it directly to bypass visibility, type checks or lazy initialization.

Check how `src/class.zig` installs each callback and compare its signature with the target's `Zend/zend_object_handlers.h`. Exercise reads, writes, exceptions, destructor reentry and final object destruction.
